        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "In the face of a critical power shortage, the grid's boundary-crossing guardian—the Philippines grid operator—moved to stabilize the system by implementing emergency measures. Officials navigated the crisis by ordering load shedding, a grid stabilization action designed to protect a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line from overloading. This response, triggered after a power unit failure and compounded by multiple plant outages and seasonal heat pushing demand into new frontiers of stress, left the Visayas region under a red alert, resulting in a significant power shortfall at the frontier with over 950 megawatts of power capacity unavailable.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
            "fragments": [
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "how-2",
            "channel": "toned",
