          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.85
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "The Visayas region faces a severe energy deficit, a massive power shortfall that emerged when the grid operator declared a red alert and officials ordered emergency restrictions on demand. This state of crisis originated from a unit's untimely journey offline—a critical power unit failure—which joined a pattern of cumulative boundary breaches across multiple plant outages. The seasonal heat, which pushed the grid into new frontiers of stress, further drove demand into a thin operating margin, ultimately leaving a massive deficit caging the grid with more than 950 megawatts unavailable.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
            "fragments": [
              "why-0",
              "why-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "result-0",
