            "salience_rank": 0
          },
          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.85
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "System regulators, acting as emergency response architects, executed a precision load-reduction design. This controlled power curtailment was a deliberate measure to prevent a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line from overloading, a direct response to the equipment failure that had reduced available capacity. The action represented a calculated intervention, a piece of crisis engineering meant to stabilize the grid and manage the resulting power shortage, even as it meant a planned disconnection of service.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Creator",
            "fragments": [
              "why-0",
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "how-2",
            "channel": "toned",
            "channel_role": "toned",
            "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
            "salience_rank": 1
          },
          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.78
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "From the vantage of the grid system orchestrator, the event began with the sudden system failure of a power unit, an initial equipment failure that shattered the operational design. This malfunction, occurring amid prolonged plant failures and a seasonal heatwave, forced an immediate reassessment. The orchestrator's focus shifted to the core problem: a critical loss of generation capacity that demanded a swift, architectural response to prevent cascading grid instability.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Creator",
            "fragments": [
              "why-0",
              "why-1",
              "why-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "why-0",
