          "id": "p1",
          "text": "When the initial trigger event—a critical mechanism failed at Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2—the grid orchestrator was forced to activate the system's alarm, placing the Visayas under red alert. This high-level grid warning was a direct response to a massive power deficit exposed, as over 950 megawatts became unavailable. The sequence reveals how a single vulnerability in the energy infrastructure can cascade, requiring the centralized power utility to deploy a grid management action to stabilize the network against collapse.",
