          "id": "p2",
          "text": "The hidden lever of demand pressure—seasonal heat pushing consumption to the brink—exposed a systemic fragility long before the grid incident. Pre-existing equipment downtime across multiple power plants had already thinned the operating margin. This climate-induced demand surge created the precise conditions where a single unit failure could trigger a grid-wide emergency, revealing the delicate balance the energy sector entity must constantly manage.",
