          "text": "A significant capacity shortfall materialized when the grid management authority, reacting to the tripped unit, initiated an emergency load management action. This data-driven escalation protocol was a calculated grid protection measure to prevent overloading a critical 230-kilovolt line, leaving more than 950 megawatts unavailable across the Visayas island group. The sequence, driven by verified weather-driven load stress and pre-existing generation shortfalls, demonstrates a clear cause-then-effect response to a quantified power deficit.",
